  "_about": "Explainer bed 'Study'. F Lydian, 84 BPM, 4/4, two seamless 16-bar loops: loop_a (pad + pluck) and loop_b (the same plus a light bass). Each loop is rendered cold, played through its release tails, and the tails are added back onto its downbeat, so the file loops end to end. Render: cargo run --release -p auracle-wasm --example score -- www/video/sound/study.json <out_dir>.",
  "_harmony": "| Fmaj7 | G6/F | Em7 | Am7 |, four times per loop. Pad (5 voices, roots included because loop_a has no bass): F3 A3 C4 E4 G4 (Fmaj9) | F3 B3 D4 E4 G4 | E3 B3 D4 E4 G4 | A2 A3 C4 E4 G4. E4 and G4 hold for the whole cycle; A3-C4 rise to B3-D4 and fall back in parallel thirds, F3 steps to E3 and drops to A2. The B natural over F in bar 2 is the Lydian #4. Every note is re-struck at the top of each 4-bar cycle, so the loop point is the same kind of join as the three inside the loop.",
